    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23663" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεικ-τικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>able to show</i>: in Logic, of syllogisms, <i>those
				which can be directly reduced,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APr.</u>
				45a24
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἐνθύμημα,</span> opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλεγκτικόν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1396b24
			</span></i>. Adv.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>APr.</u>
					29a31
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>categorical,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρότασις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Stoic.</u>
					2.85
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Gramm.,
				<i>demonstrative,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ "τοῦτο" δεικτικόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chrysipp.Stoic.
					2.65
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ὄνομα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.T.
					636.12
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρθρα</span> Apollod.Ath.and
				D.T.ap.A.D.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Pron.</u>
				5.19
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντωνυμία</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				9.17
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτεραι γιγνόμεναι</span> (sc.
